| `scripts/jobs/review_docs.py` | Judges every governed document's `updated:` stamp against the author date (`%as`) of its last commit, and lists backticked paths that resolve to nothing and thoughts in a shipped document that open with a change phrase. Its separate Markdown grammar blanks HTML block types 1 to 7 and is pinned equal to the structure scanner; types 6 and 7 end before a blank line. | `make check-docs` | [`scripts/jobs/review_docs.py --strict`](settings.md#command-line-flags), [`change_comments.phrases`](settings.md#configprojectjson) | Stale stamps fail only under `--strict`; unresolved mentions and change openers stay advisory, since a change phrase at an opener is as often a present claim. No git is a stated skip. | [doc-style.md](../guides/doc-style.md) | always |
